\cf2 \cb3 \'a0Why it matters
\f1\b0 : Nonces and permissions checks ensure that the request comes from a trusted source, protecting against security threats like CSRF (Cross-Site Request Forgery) attacks.\

\f2\i Please\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://developer.wordpress.org/apis/security/nonces/"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 \strokec6 check the official WordPress docs on nonces}}\'a0and\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://developer.wordpress.org/news/2023/08/understand-and-use-wordpress-nonces-properly/#when-to-use-nonces"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 \strokec6 this article}}\'a0for details \'97 this is a quick summary.
\f1\i0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

